<ArticleLayout
  title="How we test and pick"
  description="How Latchkey Daily chooses what it recommends: we set each tool up for a real family member, score it on the things that matter to a Gen X household, pick before we know what pays, and re-test every six months."
  eyebrow="Recommends"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Recommends', href: '/recommends/' }, { name: 'How we test', href: '/recommends/how-we-test/' }]}
  answer="We set every tool up the way a reader would: on our own phones and, where it applies, on a parent's. We score on five things, pick before we look at affiliate terms, and say on every page which links pay us."
  keyFacts={[
    'Every pick is set up on a real device by a real person on the team, including a parent\'s device where the category calls for it.',
    'Five criteria: does it work for a non-technical person, does it work for a parent you set it up for, what happens when you are locked out, what does it cost over three years, and what does the company do with your data.',
    'We decide the pick first and apply to affiliate programs second. A product that pays nothing can still be the pick, and has been.',
    'Re-tested every six months or when the product changes materially; the verified date is on every page.',
  ]}
  published="2027-02-01"
  updated="2027-02-01"
  isArticle={false}
  related={[{ title: 'Affiliate disclosure', href: '/recommends/disclosure/' }, { title: 'Editorial policy', href: '/about/editorial-policy/' }]}
  signupSource="how-we-test"
>
  <h2>What we will not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Accept payment for a placement or a rating</li>
    <li>Recommend a product we have not set up ourselves</li>
    <li>Let a sponsor see a review before it publishes</li>
    <li>Hide a commission. Every page with a paid link says so at the top</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>If we get it wrong</h2>
  <p>Tell us at <a href="/about/contact/">the contact page</a>. Reader reports that a tool has changed trigger a re-test, and corrections are logged on the <a href="/about/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
